# 佳成的挑战日记 · 照片转撕纸

For a user-submitted photograph with no text instruction, run the torn-paper workflow immediately. Do not ask “what should I do with this image?” or require a slash command.

Load `skills/torn-paper/SKILL.md` and its required references (or invoke the installed `torn-paper` skill). Choose the photo's original aspect ratio and colors automatically, plan four different tears, and call the available native reference-image generation tool once per variant. Display four real separate images; a prompt, analysis, or contact sheet is not the deliverable.

For subsequent photo-only turns, process only the newly submitted photos. An explicit different request takes precedence. Screenshots, diagrams and documents do not automatically request artwork. Images read from disk during other work or generated by the model are not new user requests.

If there is no photo, request one briefly. If the actual generation tool is unavailable or quota is exhausted, explain the concrete blocker. Do not invent outputs, configure external APIs, install dependencies, read unrelated files, or publish photos. Follow the skill's safety and retry limits.

This rule is intended for a dedicated photo studio or a project-scoped plugin. Disabling it restores the host's ordinary routing. It does not bypass host permissions.
